msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30092"
msgid "Configure base hardware parameters: region, BIOS selection, memory cards, etc."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30093"
msgid "Specify which region the system is from. 'NTSC' is 60 Hz while 'PAL' is 50 Hz. 'Auto' will detect the region of the currently loaded content. Games may run faster or slower than normal if the incorrect region is selected."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30094"
msgid "Auto"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30095"
msgid "Specify which BIOS to use. 'Auto' will attempt to load a real bios file from the frontend 'system' directory, falling back to high level emulation if unavailable. 'HLE' forces high level BIOS emulation. It is recommended to use an official bios file for better compatibility."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30096"
msgid "When using a custom BIOS file, enables the display of its file name in the OSD. Also specifies whether to show the BIOS logo when starting or selecting Reset. Warning: Enabling the logo may reduce game compatibility."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30097"
msgid "ON, w/o PCSXtm"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30098"
msgid "How to emulate the memory card in slot 1. 'Libretro' passes the card data to the frontend (usually saved as .srm). 'Game Code' saves it to a file named based on the serial, such as SCUS-00001_1.mcd, for compatibility with some other emulators."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30099"
msgid "Libretro (Default)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30100"
msgid "Game Code (Serial)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30101"
msgid "Shared Between All Games"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30102"
msgid "No Memory Card"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30103"
msgid "Same as above, but card in slot 2."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30104"
msgid "Reads the specified amount of sectors ahead of time to try to avoid later stalls. Affects both physical CD-ROM and CD images. 333000 will try to read the complete disk (requires an additional 750MB of RAM)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30105"
msgid "Dynamically recompile PSX CPU instructions to native instructions. Much faster than using an interpreter, but may be less accurate on some platforms."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30106"
msgid "Run the dynarec on another thread."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30107"
msgid "Overclock or under-clock the PSX CPU. Should be much less than 100 (something like 57) due to some real hardware slowdowns not being emulated. Usually should be left at 'Auto', else glitches or hangs are likely."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30108"
msgid "Video"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30109"
msgid "Configure base display parameters."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30110"
msgid "Enable emulation of the dithering technique used by the PSX to smooth out color banding artifacts. \"Force\" enables it even if the game turns it off. Increases performance requirements."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30111"
msgid "Force"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30112"
msgid "When enabled, runs GPU commands in a secondary thread. 'Auto' enables it if at least 2 CPU cores are detected."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30113"
msgid "Skip frames to avoid audio buffer under-run (crackling). Improves performance at the expense of visual smoothness. 'Auto' skips frames when advised by the frontend. 'Auto (Threshold)' utilises the 'Frameskip Threshold (%)' setting. 'Fixed Interval' utilises the 'Frameskip Interval' setting."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30114"
msgid "Auto (Threshold)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30115"
msgid "Fixed Interval"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30116"
msgid "When 'Frameskip' is set to 'Auto (Threshold)', specifies the audio buffer occupancy threshold (percentage) below which frames will be skipped. Higher values reduce the risk of crackling by causing frames to be dropped more frequently."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30117"
msgid "Specify the maximum number of frames that can be skipped before a new frame is rendered."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30118"
msgid "Show the internal frame rate at which the emulated system is rendering content. Note: Requires on-screen notifications to be enabled in the libretro frontend."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30119"
msgid "Shows things like unsafe hack options that are enabled and the BIOS name that is booting."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30120"
msgid "Instead of the exact 50 or 60 (maximum) fps for PAL/NTSC the real console runs closer to something like 49.75 and 59.81fps (varies slightly between hw versions). PCSX-ReARMed uses the former \"round\" framerates to better match modern displays, however that may cause audio/video desync in games like DDR and Spyro 2 (intro). With this option you can try to use fractional framerates."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30121"
msgid "Some games make changes to the framebuffer while it's being sent to the display, which is currently not emulated. However this option allows to choose if the emulator takes the video frame before the emulated PSX active display period ('Early') or after ('Late'). Normally this should be left at 'Auto'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30122"
msgid "Early"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30123"
msgid "Late"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30124"
msgid "Improves color depth for true color modes (most FMVs and occasional title screens). Causes higher CPU usage due to double memory bandwidth requirement, even in 15bpp modes. Takes effect on game reload only (libretro limitation)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30125"
msgid "When enabled, games that run in high resolution video modes (480i, 512i) will be downscaled to 320x240 by skipping lines and/or columns. May be useful on some devices with native 240p display resolutions that lack efficient hardware scaling."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30126"
msgid "Slower but more accurate GPU linked list processing. Needed by only a few games like Vampire Hunter D. Should be autodetected in most cases."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30127"
msgid "The PSX can display graphics way into the horizontal borders, even if most screens would crop it. This option tries to display all such graphics. Note that this may result in unusual resolutions that your device might not handle well. The 'Hack' option is intended for the widescreen hacks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30128"
msgid "Hack"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30129"
msgid "The PSX has a feature allowing it to shift the image position on screen. Some (mostly PAL) games used this feature in a strange way making the image miscentered and causing uneven borders to appear. With 'Auto' the emulator tries to correct this miscentering automatically. 'Game-controlled' uses the settings supplied by the game. 'Manual' allows to override those values with the settings below."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30130"
msgid "Game-controlled"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30131"
msgid "Borderless"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30132"
msgid "Manual"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30133"
msgid "X offset of the frame buffer. Only effective when 'Screen centering' is set to 'Manual'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30134"
msgid "Y offset of the frame buffer. Only effective when 'Screen centering' is set to 'Manual'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30135"
msgid "Height adjustment. Only effective when 'Screen centering' is set to 'Manual'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30136"
msgid "GPU Plugin"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30137"
msgid "Configure low-level settings of the NEON GPU plugin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30138"
msgid "When enabled, games that run in high resolution video modes (480i, 512i) will produced interlaced video output. While this displays correctly on CRT televisions, it will produce artifacts on modern displays. When disabled, all video is output in progressive format. Note: there are games that will glitch is this is off."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30139"
msgid "Render games that do not already run in high resolution video modes (480i, 512i) at twice the native internal resolution. Improves the fidelity of 3D models at the expense of increased performance requirements. 2D elements are generally unaffected by this setting."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30140"
msgid "('Enhanced Resolution' Hack) Improves performance but reduces compatibility and may cause rendering errors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30141"
msgid "('Enhanced Resolution' Hack) Solves some texturing issues in some games in Enhanced Resolution mode. May cause a small performance hit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30142"
msgid "GPU Plugin (Advanced)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30143"
msgid "Configure low-level settings of the P.E.Op.S. GPU plugin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30144"
msgid "A hack fix used to correct lock-ups that may occur in games such as Chrono Cross. Disable unless required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30145"
msgid "Intended for use only with Capcom 2D fighting games. Enlarges the display area at the right side of the screen to show all background elements without cut-off. May cause rendering errors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30146"
msgid "A hack fix used to repair black screens in Lunar Silver Star Story Complete when entering a house or a menu. Disable unless required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30147"
msgid "Legacy compatibility mode. May improve games that fail to run correctly on newer GPU hardware. Disable unless required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30148"
msgid "A partial fix to prevent text box flickering in Dragon Warrior VII. May also improve Pandemonium 2. Disable unless required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30149"
msgid "A hack fix used to correct rendering errors in Star Wars: Dark Forces. Disable unless required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30150"
msgid "Corrects graphical distortions that may occur when games utilize Gouraud Shading, at the expense of reduced texture quality. Disable unless required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30151"
msgid "Emulate the 'GPU is busy' (drawing primitives) status flag of the original hardware instead of assuming the GPU is always ready for commands. May improve compatibility at the expense of reduced performance. Disable unless required."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30152"
msgid "Configure low-level settings of the UNAI GPU plugin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30153"
msgid "This enables faster, but less accurate code."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30154"
msgid "Enable alpha-based (and additive) texture blending. Required for various rendering effects, including transparency (e.g. water, shadows). Can be disabled to improve performance at the expense of severe display errors/inaccuracies."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30155"
msgid "Skips every second scanline. Can be enabled to improve performance at the expense of display inaccuracies (artifacts etc.)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30156"
msgid "Enable simulated lighting effects (via vertex coloring combined with texture mapping). Required by almost all 3D games. Can be disabled to improve performance at the expense of severe display errors/inaccuracies (missing shadows, flat textures, etc.)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30157"
msgid "Improves performance when 'Lighting Effects' are enabled, but may cause moderate/severe rendering errors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30158"
msgid "Audio"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30159"
msgid "Configure sound emulation: reverb, interpolation, CD audio decoding."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30160"
msgid "Enable emulation of the reverb feature provided by the PSX SPU. Can be disabled to improve performance at the expense of reduced audio quality/authenticity."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30161"
msgid "Enable emulation of the in-built audio interpolation provided by the PSX SPU. 'Gaussian' sounds closest to original hardware. 'Simple' improves performance but reduces quality. 'Cubic' has the highest performance requirements but produces increased clarity. Can be disabled entirely for maximum performance, at the expense of greatly reduced audio quality."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30162"
msgid "Simple"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30163"
msgid "Gaussian"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30164"
msgid "Cubic"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30165"
msgid "disabled"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30166"
msgid "Enable playback of CD (CD-DA) audio tracks. Can be disabled to improve performance in games that include CD audio, at the expense of missing music."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30167"
msgid "Enable playback of XA (eXtended Architecture ADPCM) audio tracks. Can be disabled to improve performance in games that include XA audio, at the expense of missing music."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30168"
msgid "Emulates the PSX SPU on another CPU thread. May cause audio glitches in some games."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30169"
msgid "Input"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30170"
msgid "Configure input devices: analog response, haptic feedback, Multitaps, light guns, etc."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30171"
msgid "Specify range limits for the left and right analog sticks when input device is set to 'analog' or 'dualshock'. 'Square' bounds improve input response when using controllers with highly circular ranges that are unable to fully saturate the X and Y axes at 45 degree deflections."
msgstr ""

